  "worked_solution": "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({x}^{2}+1)^{x})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡((1-3x)^{5}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-3x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot (2x)-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-3x}\\cdot (-3) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{15}{1-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{15}{1-3x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)+\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{15}{1-3x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{15}{1-3x})+\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}(\\frac{2{x}^{2}(1-3x)+15({x}^{2}+1)}{({x}^{2}+1)(1-3x)})+\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}(\\frac{17{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3}+15}{({x}^{2}+1)(1-3x)})+\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x-1}}{(1-3x)^{6}}(17{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3}+15)+\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)^{x}}{(1-3x)^{5}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x)=17{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3}+15.\n$$",
